BMW has rolls-royce and Audi has Bentley  but what does the other German luxury  car maker have to offer after the credit  crisis killed Maybach diamonds on your  CD z' but now Daimler is going to bring  back the Pullman version of its  top-of-the-line s-class plated with  armor it costs over a million dollars  more than twice the price of the most  expensive rolls-royce aimed at royalty  and the ridiculously rich the Mercedes  s-class Pohlman is what we hear in  America actually think of as a limousine  with two rows of seats facing each other  in the back and a chauffeur's cabin  separated by a privacy screen the  Pullman is going to be about 21 feet  long making it about the same size as a  great white shark that makes it the  biggest production passenger car in the  world the car is meant to invoke the  famous Mercedes 600 series limousines  used to show for the likes of the Pope  and Elvis Presley it was owned by  celebrities like John Lennon and Jeremy  Clarkson Daimler aims to overtake BMW as  the biggest luxury car maker in the  world by the end of the decade but  meeting this goal requires Mercedes  perversely to produce much cheaper cars  like the $29,000 CLA in order to boost  volume but Mercedes has to be careful to  keep that luxury luster and it's doing  so with a line of huge high margin halo  cars based on the Mercedes flagship  s-class maybe they need to balance out  the bottom end with these unattainable  luxury cars will even work its magic on  Maybach there are rumors we're going to  see that nameplate on a Mercedes at a  couple of car shows in November
 

